{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.FluidDynamics.dss_escapes_nrs","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.dss_escapes_nrs","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.selfSimilar_isDSS","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.selfSimilar_isDSS","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/dss_escapes_nrs.lean#L89-L96","doc":"**The steady class is the strict floor.** Any self-similar profile is DSS for\nevery period (its `s`-independence is the degenerate case of periodicity);\nthe content of the re-scope is that the converse fails — non-steady\nsingle-period profiles exist in principle and are what NRŠ leaves open. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.dss_not_selfSimilar_of_nonconstant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.dss_not_selfSimilar_of_nonconstant","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/dss_escapes_nrs.lean#L78-L87","doc":"**Single-period DSS is not steady** (given a non-constant value). A DSS\nprofile that takes some value `≠ U 0` is not self-similar — so it lies in the\ncomplement of the NRŠ-excluded steady class and is not touched by the no-go.\nThis is the class the discretely-self-similar re-scope lives in. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.selfSimilar_iff_all_periods","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.selfSimilar_iff_all_periods","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/dss_escapes_nrs.lean#L65-L76","doc":"**Steady = periodic for every period.** A similarity profile is\n(continuously) self-similar iff it is discretely self-similar for *every*\nperiod `P`. Hence the NRŠ-excluded steady class is precisely the intersection\nof all the DSS classes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.DSSPeriodic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.DSSPeriodic","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/dss_escapes_nrs.lean#L60-L63","doc":"The similarity profile `U(s)` is **discretely self-similar** with period `P`\nif it is `P`-periodic in `s` (`P = 2 log λ_κ` for the root-of-unity scaling\n`λ_κ`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.SelfSimilar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.SelfSimilar","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/dss_escapes_nrs.lean#L55-L58","doc":"The similarity profile `U(s)` is **(continuously) self-similar** if it is\nindependent of the similarity time `s` (steady). This is the class NRŠ\nexcludes for finite energy. ","signatureChunk":0}]}